  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "Great — here is a comprehensive overview of the soft-brand and collection options most commonly considered by hotel owners seeking a conversion in the Caribbean and Latin America (CALA):\n\n---\n\n## Soft Brand & Collection Options for Hotel Conversions in the Caribbean & Latin America\n\nConversions have become a major growth driver across the CALA region. \nConversions represented 32% of total room signings in the Caribbean and Latin America in recent years.\n Below are the key brands and collections that owners most frequently consider:\n\n---\n\n### 🏨 **Marriott International**\nMarriott is one of the most active players in CALA conversions and offers a strong roster of soft brands and conversion-friendly options:\n\n- \nMarriott has continued to see strong momentum in the space, owing to many of its conversion-friendly brands across segments, like **The Luxury Collection**, **Autograph Collection Hotels**, **Tribute Portfolio**, **Delta Hotels**, and **Four Points by Sheraton**.\n\n\n- \nAccording to Jose Gonzalez, VP for Development at Marriott International in the Caribbean and Latin America, they offer a unique value proposition for owners and franchisees and deliver momentum for their robust portfolio of soft brands and conversion-friendly brands in the region. Conversions represented 32% of total room signings in the region, including brands like **Autograph Collection Hotels**, **The Luxury Collection**, and **Tribute Portfolio**.\n\n\n---\n\n### 🏨 **Hilton**\nHilton has positioned soft brands as a central pillar of its CALA conversion strategy:\n\n- \nHilton is seeing traction with hotel conversion opportunities. Along with using its conversion-oriented brands that are more nimble and agile, such as **Curio Collection** or **Tapestry Collection**, it's also finding success with some of its brands in higher segments, such as **DoubleTree by Hilton**.\n\n\n- \nHilton is opening the **Zemi Miches Punta Cana All-Inclusive Resort, Curio Collection by Hilton** in the Dominican Republic, illustrating the brand's active use in the region.\n\n\n- \nThe company foresees both its soft-brand collections and the all-inclusive resort segment as opportunities for further growth, with brands that can \"easily adapt\" to allow for conversions of existing resorts.\n\n\n---\n\n### 🏨 **IHG Hotels & Resorts**\nIHG has made soft brands and conversions a primary engine of growth throughout CALA:\n\n- \nIHG provides a range of choices for travelers in the region, with luxury offerings such as **Six Senses** as well as select-service brands such as **Holiday Inn Express**, **Avid**, and **Garner**, one of its soft brands. The company's soft-brand and conversion-friendly brands have helped to drive growth in the region.\n\n\n- \nIHG signed two **Vignette Collection** properties in CALA and opened one in Peru, with another opening in the Dominican Republic. The **Voco** brand brings recognition that many owners want without having to create a new identity for the hotel.\n\n\n- \nThe **voco** brand notably reopened in Hermosillo, Mexico, in late 2024 following an extensive conversion.\n\n\n---\n\n### 🏨 **Accor**\nAccor has been particularly active with its collection brands in conversions globally, and is making inroads into the Caribbean specifically:\n\n- \nWith its diverse array of collection brands and seamless approach towards reflagging, Accor is a top choice of investors for conversion projects. Approximately 55% of Accor's projects in 2025 have been conversions, with brands such as **Emblems Collection**, **MGallery Collection**, and **Handwritten Collection** leading the way.\n\n\n- \nOther conversion-ready brands from the Group include **Mercure**, **Mövenpick**, **greet**, and **TRIBE**, as well as brands from Ennismore including **Hyde**.\n\n\n- \nAccor announced **The Whimsy Hotel & Spa Saint-Martin – MGallery Collection**, which will be the first MGallery hotel in the Caribbean, marking a strategic milestone for the boutique-hotel collection's growth.\n\n\n- \nAccor's collection portfolio spans multiple price tiers: **MGallery Hotel Collection** (upper upscale), **Emblems Collection** (luxury), and **Handwritten Collection** (midscale).\n\n\n---\n\n### 🏨 **Hyatt**\nHyatt is also growing aggressively in the CALA region, particularly in the all-inclusive and lifestyle segments:\n\n- \nHyatt's strategy includes the Hyatt Ziva and Hyatt Zilara brands, the acquisition of Apple Leisure Group in 2021, and a 50/50 joint venture with Grupo Piñero in 2024, which brought **Bahia Principe Hotels & Resorts** into Hyatt's **Inclusive Collection** — the largest portfolio of luxury all-inclusive resorts in the world.\n\n\n- \nHyatt is also bringing its new **Hyatt Vivid** brand, a lifestyle all-inclusive, to the Dominican Republic.\n\n\n---\n\n### Summary Table\n\n| Brand Family | Key Soft/Collection Brands for CALA Conversions |\n|---|---|\n| **Marriott** | Autograph Collection, The Luxury Collection, Tribute Portfolio |\n| **Hilton** | Curio Collection, Tapestry Collection, DoubleTree |\n| **IHG** | Vignette Collection, Voco, Garner |\n| **Accor** | MGallery, Emblems Collection, Handwritten Collection, Hyde (Ennismore) |\n| **Hyatt** | Inclusive Collection, Hyatt Vivid, Hyatt Ziva/Zilara |\n\nIn short, \npost-pandemic, more owners in the region have started to understand the importance of branding\n, and the breadth of soft/collection options from these major hospitality groups means that independent hoteliers at virtually every price point and property type can find a conversion-friendly brand suited to their asset.",
